{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"paranormal-corporeal-illadopsis","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\noutbound_differ.py sits at 799/800 LOC (the hard module-size cap; CI-only gate in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml, limit .github/module-size-limit.txt=800). S2 (438a) drove it to 799 via repo_root threading. S3 (a8ea, type mapping) and S6 (d458) both must ADD code to it — S3 needs a rebar-type: stamp invocation site (mirroring the rebar-status: stamp invoked ~line 763) and per-project type-skip threading through compute_outbound_mutations (~line 374, where EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES is loaded and passed to _compute_outbound_select_absent_gets). Any addition breaches 800 and fails CI Verified.\n\n## Approach\nSplit outbound_differ.py along an EXISTING call-graph seam (never mechanically) into two files each 200-500 LOC, per AGENTS.md module-size policy. Candidate seams: the absent-alive-GET pre-selection cluster (_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets + helpers) or the annotation-mutation cluster (~line 763, _EXCLUDED_PREFIXES-based label diffing). Behavior-preserving extraction only; keep public API (compute_outbound_mutations, OutboundDiffConfig) stable. tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py mirrors the gate.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py (extract a cluster)\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/<new module> (the extracted cluster)\n- any importer of the moved symbols\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] outbound_differ.py and the new module are each < 800 LOC (verify: find src/rebar -name '*.py' | xargs wc -l | awk '$1>800').\n- [ ] The reconciler suite (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/, tests touching outbound_differ) passes GREEN — pure behavior-preserving refactor, no observable change.\n- [ ] The extraction follows an existing call-graph seam (no <100-LOC fragment created).\n\nTest tier: refactor — existing outbound_differ suite is the oracle (no new behavior). Discovered during S3 (a8ea) plan-review round 1 (6 G1G2/G6 blocking findings), which established S3 must add to outbound_differ.py.","id":"f1bc-75f6-ed8c-472f","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Split outbound_differ.py below module-size cap (prerequisite for S3/S6)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787345850922432001,"uuid":"ffd9ec21-10fb-4c6c-b3b2-fa8c6ea0cd7c"}